1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
How do you like that?

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
I may be a commoner, but I won!

6
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Yeah! How do you like that?

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Hey, man, are you alright?

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,000
He is such a fool, and a reckless one at that.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
About time you woke up, you sadistic jerks.

10
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
This spell of his appears to be blocking my magic.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Just wait, you're gonna spill everything.

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Who you people are, what you're after.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The magic knights will get every last scrap of information out of you!

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,000
They will not.

15
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,000
The end times are upon us.

16
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Engage ice magic, ice burial.

17
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,000
They're real.

18
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
You weren't willing to go that far?

19
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,000
What was he thinking?

20
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,000
How could they?

21
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Treating life like it's something to throw away!

22
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,000
No way!

23
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,000
No way!

24
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,000
No way!

25
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,000
No way!

26
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,000
No way!

27
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Never mind!

28
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,000
No way!

29
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,000
No way!

30
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,000
No way!

31
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
No way!

32
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
..

33
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,000
..

34
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,600
言葉なんてじゃ何ひとつ叶わない

35
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:07,700
わかってる? わかってるんだ

36
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:09,400
獣王不� internet

37
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:12,300
どこまでも 幅かけたらな

38
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:15,400
何処の日を夢みてた

39
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:17,500
それでも一歩いおすかしいから

40
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:20,100
世界でも何度も過ごれた分

41
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:23,260
そっこの王 のままあくりました

42
00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:30,400
遥か未来へ 今駆け出したんだ

43
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:35,980
未来的不安さを全て超えて

44
00:02:35,980 --> 00:02:40,960
あの日描いた僕が僕であるために

45
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:46,220
見つづけてページの続けが来よう

46
00:02:46,220 --> 00:02:49,860
君の言う希望という

47
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:52,440
まるでいつかのワンプエンジのような

48
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:55,120
君と僕が出会えた

49
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:58,020
これを防ぎって呼ぼうか

50
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:30,380
To be continued...

51
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:31,920
He was a man of laughter.

52
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:34,240
Come on, let's laugh for the old guy.

53
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:37,660
Your turn.

54
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:40,960
That's it.

55
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:44,160
Come on, Nono.

56
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:53,920
Okay, that's enough.

57
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:57,460
It's a real shame what happened to Sehi.

58
00:03:58,320 --> 00:04:00,220
But you protected the villagers.

59
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:04,160
Hold your heads high.

60
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,320
You did a good job.

61
00:04:08,780 --> 00:04:10,620
So be proud of yourselves, you idiots.

62
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:12,220
Sir!

63
00:04:13,140 --> 00:04:13,940
Thank you.

64
00:04:13,940 --> 00:04:19,280
Hey, what are you doing with your hand?

65
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:20,480
Are you kidding me?

66
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:23,000
You seriously don't know the Magic Knight Salute?

67
00:04:23,460 --> 00:04:24,760
Well, take a good look.

68
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:27,960
These fingers represent the three leaves of a clover.

69
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:29,520
Go on, you try.

70
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,020
Does this look right?

71
00:04:31,380 --> 00:04:33,020
Yeah, not bad.

72
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,440
We're back.

73
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:41,040
We heard about Saucy Village.

74
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:42,100
Good work out there.

75
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:43,020
Thanks.

76
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:45,020
It was a tough mission, but we did our best.

77
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:48,080
We visited the Magic Investigation Department, Captain.

78
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:49,720
Yeah, good.

79
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:51,020
Did you learn anything?

80
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:53,340
Like who the hell that guy was?

81
00:04:53,340 --> 00:04:55,540
I'll find his hideout and tear it apart.

82
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,240
And the same thing goes for the one that got away.

83
00:04:58,640 --> 00:04:59,820
Yeah, about that guy.

84
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:04,980
The investigators checked the area and went over the things he left behind.

85
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:07,000
But so far, no dice.

86
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:09,320
What good are they then?

87
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:14,340
That's enough.

88
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:15,560
Hear me?

89
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:17,660
Quit breaking everything!

90
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:20,560
Sizer!

91
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:24,300
That pocket watch was pretty nice.

92
00:05:24,420 --> 00:05:26,100
Not something just anybody would own.

93
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:27,180
That's true.

94
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:33,500
Also, based on the remarks he made about commoners, I'd say we're looking at someone of fairly high rank.

95
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,320
Royalty, or at least nobility.

96
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:39,360
Oh!

97
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:40,840
Who's this?

98
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:42,080
Cutie pie!

99
00:05:42,180 --> 00:05:43,700
What's so cute about this pest?

100
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,320
Um, only everything!

101
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:48,640
Hey!

102
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:50,460
Come here, little one.

103
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:54,420
Ugly, feathered little nuisance!

104
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,540
I'm gonna fry you up for dinner!

105
00:05:57,180 --> 00:05:59,040
I won't play so much as a finger on him!

106
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:01,400
Say your prayers, birdie!

107
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:03,940
I told you to leave him alone!

108
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:07,160
Are you two trying to destroy the whole building here?

109
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:09,920
Sorry, Captain, sir!

110
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:13,540
Although you're the one who's doing most of the damage.

111
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:16,520
Okay, everybody, shut up and listen.

112
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:21,840
Doesn't make a difference if the guy is royalty, nobility, or whatever.

113
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:25,860
We'll leave the investigation to the pros and wait for the report to come in.

114
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:27,300
Now that's settled.

115
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:29,740
I've got some good news for you.

116
00:06:30,100 --> 00:06:31,460
Good news about what?

117
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:33,040
You wanna hear?

118
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:34,240
Yeah, of course we do!

119
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:40,720
Believe it or not, the Wizard King himself has recognized your efforts.

120
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:41,760
The Wizard King?

121
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:45,400
For your work in Saucy Village, he awarded us a star.

122
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:46,360
A star?

123
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:47,900
Seriously?

124
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:49,900
Who was?

125
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:52,220
We got a star!

126
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:53,760
Wow, nice.

127
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:55,040
Congrats, you three.

128
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:57,940
So, what does the star mean?

129
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:00,280
You're celebrating when you don't even know?

130
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:01,320
It's a symbol.

131
00:07:01,860 --> 00:07:04,520
The Wizard King gives them to people who perform great deeds.

132
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:05,420
Oh, wow!

133
00:07:05,520 --> 00:07:06,480
So what's it good for?

134
00:07:06,860 --> 00:07:09,500
Uh, well, I mean, it's an honor.

135
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:10,660
That's so awesome!

136
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:12,380
You get it now?

137
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:13,380
It's an honor.

138
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:15,220
A real medal for us real men.

139
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:16,920
And woman, too, don't forget.

140
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:19,060
A medal for us real men and woman!

141
00:07:19,220 --> 00:07:20,860
They make no sense half the time.

142
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:22,400
It's a competition, too.

143
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:24,800
The squads all vie to see who can get the most.

144
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:27,300
It's an indicator of a squad's achievement.

145
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:29,620
The more stars you have, the more successful you are.

146
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:32,180
Whoa, I guess they're a really big deal then, huh?

147
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:36,480
Right now, the Golden Dawn's ranked highest in terms of stars.

148
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:37,640
They've got 70.

149
00:07:38,020 --> 00:07:38,420
70?

150
00:07:38,420 --> 00:07:40,660
What about us?

151
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:42,520
How many do the Black Bulls have?

152
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:45,040
We can't be that far behind.

153
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:48,180
How many do we have?

154
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:58,940
With this one, we're officially at negative 30 now.

155
00:07:59,340 --> 00:07:59,900
Negative?

156
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:01,000
What?

157
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:04,880
Finally, an even hundred away from catching up to the dawn.

158
00:08:04,980 --> 00:08:06,140
A hundred away?

159
00:08:06,140 --> 00:08:09,240
One hundred stars?

160
00:08:09,620 --> 00:08:13,280
We have some serious catching up to do if we're going to beat your squad, you know?

161
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,240
Not happening.

162
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:18,260
How do you even get negative stars?

163
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,140
What am I doing in this squad?

164
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,260
All right, just one more thing.

165
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:26,820
Your wages for this month.

166
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:30,300
No way!

167
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:31,640
There's so much money!

168
00:08:31,980 --> 00:08:34,020
There's like 200,000 Yule here!

169
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:35,240
Thank you, Captain.

170
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:37,520
Yeah, thank you, Captain Yummy!

171
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:40,540
This will buy so many trains, it's gonna be yummy!

172
00:08:40,820 --> 00:08:42,280
Sure, eat up, Charmy.

173
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:43,900
Captain, let's make a deal.

174
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:46,180
How much do I have to give you for you to fight me?

175
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:47,760
Come on, name your price.

176
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:48,880
Give it up, kid.

177
00:08:49,340 --> 00:08:50,700
Oh, that's no fair!

178
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:55,720
Now that we've been paid, I'd like to use the money to buy some clothes from my angelic little sister, Marie.

179
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:57,660
What do you think would suit her, Captain?

180
00:08:57,920 --> 00:08:59,040
Like I would know.

181
00:08:59,620 --> 00:09:00,020
Phew.

182
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:01,600
No clue.

183
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:04,280
You've got the day off tomorrow, everybody.

184
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:06,220
Don't blow through all your wages.

185
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:08,780
I'm going to fit in as many dates as possible.

186
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:09,360
Ha!

187
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:10,700
Whatever you want.

188
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:13,620
Thanks a lot, Captain Yummy!

189
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:23,640
Barely pocket change.

190
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:25,240
Wow, are you kidding me?

191
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:28,460
This could buy 10 years worth of pot potatoes easy!

192
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:30,540
And what in the world are pot potatoes?

193
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:33,140
They're a hearty crop grown in Hodge Village.

194
00:09:33,300 --> 00:09:35,640
A bit on the lumpy side with a real subtle flavor.

195
00:09:35,980 --> 00:09:36,940
They sound disgusting.

196
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,940
Well, they're not at all!

197
00:09:38,940 --> 00:09:41,720
Everything that Sister Lily cooks with them comes out great!

198
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:42,980
Who is that?

199
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:46,420
The beautiful woman I've decided I'm going to marry someday!

200
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:47,080
What?

201
00:09:47,700 --> 00:09:49,640
Sister means she's a woman of the cloth.

202
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:51,380
You do know they can't marry.

203
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:51,740
Ha!

204
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:53,880
I'll make it work somehow!

205
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:56,160
It's all about surpassing my limits!

206
00:09:56,340 --> 00:09:57,400
Are you insane?

207
00:09:57,980 --> 00:10:00,060
Congratulations on your first payday!

208
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:02,300
So, whatcha gonna spend it on?

209
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:04,320
Nothing special.

210
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:06,120
What about you?

211
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:08,240
Oh, I'm sending it to the church.

212
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:10,320
Back in Hodge, where I'm from.

213
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:10,820
Good!

214
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:12,500
That's what a real man does, Asta.

215
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:14,040
Helps his family.

216
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:15,420
Yeah, I'm pumped about it!

217
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:17,460
Are you sending yours back home too, Magna?

218
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:19,140
You bet I am!

219
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:20,440
Well, kinda.

220
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:21,340
What do you mean?

221
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:24,240
After I've got a hundred times more.

222
00:10:25,680 --> 00:10:26,880
He never learns.

223
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:28,580
Go big or go home!

224
00:10:28,620 --> 00:10:30,220
That's what a real man does!

225
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:31,620
A really stupid man?

226
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:32,800
That I believe.

227
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:35,960
It's good to help out back home, but don't send it all, kiddo.

228
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:38,020
You should use a little of it on yourself.

229
00:10:38,620 --> 00:10:40,360
Okay, I guess I can do that.

230
00:10:41,020 --> 00:10:42,820
But how exactly?

231
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:44,740
Oh, that's easy.

232
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:46,960
We'll go shopping in the castle town tomorrow.

233
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,700
It'll be so much fun.

234
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:49,520
Shopping?

235
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:50,940
I'll take care of you.

236
00:10:51,020 --> 00:10:51,840
Don't you worry.

237
00:10:51,840 --> 00:11:02,800
Dear Sister Lily, how are you?

238
00:11:03,220 --> 00:11:04,260
I'm doing great.

239
00:11:04,700 --> 00:11:06,540
The other black bulls are really nice.

240
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:07,840
They look out for me.

241
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:11,700
Alright, stand here for me a sec.

242
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:13,540
Uh, what's going on?

243
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:15,560
Just keep Ria still.

244
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:17,480
Flame magic!

245
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:20,920
Am I exploding?

246
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:21,280
I'm exploding!

247
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:25,980
Tie your bow!

248
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:34,360
I told you to keep still!

249
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:35,320
I'm trying!

250
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:36,020
I'm trying!

251
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:38,700
I'm working hard.

252
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:43,700
I did so well on my first mission that the Wizard King gave us a star as a commendation.

253
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:45,060
Isn't that awesome?

254
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:47,720
If this keeps up, who knows what could happen?

255
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:50,400
I might even be the Wizard King by next month.

256
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:56,380
Once I am, I'll make this a world where everyone can be happy, no matter where they come from.

257
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:58,680
And then, I'll come back for you.

258
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:00,600
So please, marry me.

259
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:01,640
Oh, yeah!

260
00:12:01,980 --> 00:12:04,440
I had my first payday, so I'm sending you some Yule.

261
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:05,320
There.

262
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:07,340
Letter done!

263
00:12:07,340 --> 00:12:10,340
Not too shabby, if I do say so myself.

264
00:12:10,820 --> 00:12:13,440
Sister Lily will be moved to tears when she reads it.

265
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:18,140
That's his castle.

266
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:19,820
The Wizard King.

267
00:12:19,820 --> 00:12:21,780
I wonder what he's like.

268
00:12:21,780 --> 00:12:36,940
So, have you two ever been to the castle town?

269
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:38,260
No, I haven't.

270
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:40,920
Well, that makes sense, you being royalty and all.

271
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:43,480
Your kind don't spend time with regular folk.

272
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:45,080
What about you, kiddo?

273
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:48,380
Yeah, I passed through when I came to take the Magic Knight's entrance exam.

274
00:12:49,160 --> 00:12:52,060
Well, let's make the most of our visit today.

275
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:54,620
I could do with a little less touching, please.

276
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:56,240
Come on, I can't help it.

277
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:57,540
Do you want me to fall off?

278
00:12:57,540 --> 00:13:00,720
I'm weirdly tuned to it somehow.

279
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:02,380
Not good.

280
00:13:04,460 --> 00:13:05,580
Not again!

281
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:14,100
The Clover Kingdom includes the Noble Realm, domain of royalty and nobility,

282
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:16,800
the Common Realm, where the citizenry live,

283
00:13:17,220 --> 00:13:19,560
and the Forsaken Realm, home to the commoners.

284
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:25,000
Kika, the castle town where Asta and Yuno took the Magic Knight's entrance exam,

285
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,060
is located in the Common Realm.

286
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:34,860
It's just as awesome as I remember!

287
00:13:35,300 --> 00:13:36,660
Certainly very likely.

288
00:13:36,940 --> 00:13:37,660
Ah!

289
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:49,160
It'd be really cool to bring Sister Lily and the kids from the church here someday.

290
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:52,020
What about me?

291
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:53,560
Huh?

292
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:57,440
Little Marie.

293
00:13:57,540 --> 00:13:59,080
My darling angel.

294
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:00,900
It won't be long now.

295
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:05,820
To wait another day before seeing your lovely face would be more suffering than I could endure.

296
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:15,140
Let's do this!

297
00:14:15,140 --> 00:14:17,080
I know that voice.

298
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:24,020
Back again this month, huh?

299
00:14:24,020 --> 00:14:26,060
That's right, I am.

300
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:28,520
Yeah, well this time I'm gonna win!

301
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:30,200
It's nice to have hope.

302
00:14:31,140 --> 00:14:34,520
An extra super-sized deluxe with everything on it!

303
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:36,480
You just try to finish this one!

304
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:37,480
Bring it, I'm ready!

305
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:45,800
I've got heartburn just from watching her.

306
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:46,800
Pardon Miss, are you free?

307
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:47,120
Perhaps we can grab something to drink.

308
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:48,120
Does it look like I'm free?

309
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:49,120
Does it look like I'm free?

310
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:50,120
Oh, of course!

311
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:51,120
Bring your children!

312
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:52,120
Let's go!

313
00:14:52,120 --> 00:15:01,440
I know a great li-

314
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:03,760
What do you mean, my children?

315
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:07,780
I'm their older sister, and I need to get back to help set up the shop.

316
00:15:07,780 --> 00:15:09,600
I don't have time to be fooling around.

317
00:15:11,180 --> 00:15:14,300
Oh, I do have a weakness for strong women.

318
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:15,580
Huh?

319
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:18,600
Hello, miss!

320
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:19,820
Would you care to get a drink?

321
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:24,580
Don't get too far ahead now, we might lose you.

322
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:28,160
Are you sure you haven't seen anything that you'd like to buy?

323
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:30,120
Aw, man!

324
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:32,980
There's just so much stuff here, I don't know what to pick!

325
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:34,700
Nothing's caught my eye.

326
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:37,180
Hey, see the robes?

327
00:15:37,180 --> 00:15:38,560
Those are magic knights!

328
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:42,500
And check out that symbol.

329
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:44,340
Ugh, the black bulls?

330
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:47,400
Yeah, that's Vanessa, the bottomless booze pit.

331
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:50,600
That cute girl and the kid, are they black bulls too?

332
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:53,240
Probably better to keep our distance.

333
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:57,880
They're making quite a fuss over our robes, aren't they?

334
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:59,280
Yep, don't worry though.

335
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:02,840
They know that having magic knights around is an excellent crime deterrent.

336
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:06,860
And if we're lucky, some marvelous gentleman might come over and say hello!

337
00:16:07,180 --> 00:16:13,760
Stamina restoring herbs, check.

338
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:16,940
Chic ointment for counteracting poisons, check.

339
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:17,900
Excellent.

340
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:19,660
I think that should just about do it.

341
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:22,900
I've bought the important stuff.

342
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:25,480
Now let's head somewhere a bit quieter.

343
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:27,160
What did you have in mind?

344
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:29,480
Come on, you trust me, right?

345
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:30,660
Um.

346
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:32,600
This way.

347
00:16:33,280 --> 00:16:34,500
Are you sure?

348
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:36,100
It's just some back alley.

349
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:43,960
Um, that's a dead end.

350
00:16:47,060 --> 00:16:47,660
Whoa!

351
00:16:49,020 --> 00:16:50,240
Well, are you coming?

352
00:16:51,060 --> 00:16:51,420
Huh?

353
00:16:51,420 --> 00:17:02,840
Welcome to the black market.

354
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:03,980
A black market?

355
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:04,720
Huh.

356
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:08,300
Now, I won't lie.

357
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:13,120
It may be a bit on the dangerous side, but they've got some crazy good magic items here.

358
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:16,880
Vanessa, I have some new merchandise that might interest you.

359
00:17:17,060 --> 00:17:17,940
Sounds lovely.

360
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:19,880
I'll be sure to stop by later.

361
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:20,840
So cool!

362
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:21,940
Hmm.

363
00:17:22,820 --> 00:17:23,280
Hmm.

364
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:24,920
You don't seem to be impressed.

365
00:17:25,500 --> 00:17:26,320
Not especially.

366
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:28,180
I'm not surprised.

367
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:31,900
Royals and nobles instinctively dislike this place.

368
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:34,820
But you might change your mind.

369
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:36,660
Are you still having some issues?

370
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:38,060
You know, with control?

371
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:39,540
Well, yes.

372
00:17:39,860 --> 00:17:41,040
But why does that matter?

373
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:44,360
Because, sweetie, there are items here that can suppress magic.

374
00:17:46,540 --> 00:17:49,200
Look hard and you might find just the right item.

375
00:17:49,420 --> 00:17:50,800
One to tweak your magic power?

376
00:17:51,060 --> 00:17:53,640
Then maybe you would finally be able to control it.

377
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:55,780
You really think that's possible?

378
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:58,740
Let's just see what they have, shall we?

379
00:17:59,180 --> 00:18:00,260
Yes, let's go!

380
00:18:01,900 --> 00:18:04,080
They sure are packing them in over there.

381
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:05,480
Sorry, kiddo.

382
00:18:05,780 --> 00:18:07,540
You two aren't ready for that just yet.

383
00:18:08,020 --> 00:18:11,180
Amateurs can be taken for all they've got if they aren't careful.

384
00:18:12,140 --> 00:18:13,380
All right!

385
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:15,860
We ready to get this party started?

386
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:18,700
Time to turn one payday into a hundred!

387
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:20,980
That's not gonna end well.

388
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:24,540
Damn it!

389
00:18:24,780 --> 00:18:25,660
Lost again!

390
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:31,440
Too bad for you I can see the future, dearie.

391
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:34,700
That old bat really cleaned me out.

392
00:18:35,780 --> 00:18:38,120
I guess I shouldn't be gambling anyway.

393
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:40,500
Well, back to work.

394
00:18:41,900 --> 00:18:43,220
And some work it is.

395
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:45,780
Bringing in small-time purse snatchers?

396
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:49,280
As if they really need a magic knight to do that job.

397
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:51,160
This is the worst.

398
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,240
But if I say no, I'll answer to the captain.

399
00:18:54,980 --> 00:18:56,200
Then that man's frightening.

400
00:18:57,740 --> 00:18:59,960
You don't feel like doing your job?

401
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:02,080
Then how about I tear you in two?

402
00:19:02,080 --> 00:19:07,660
I thought being a magic knight would mean doing important things.

403
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:10,660
Even if I am just a green praying mantis.

404
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:11,920
Really?

405
00:19:12,580 --> 00:19:13,580
Praying mantis?

406
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:14,920
Who wants to be a bug?

407
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:17,240
They run me ragged with odd jobs,

408
00:19:17,680 --> 00:19:18,700
finally go out on a mission,

409
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:20,200
and they use me as a decoy.

410
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:23,960
I'm constipated and my hair's starting to thin.

411
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:24,820
Okay, let's take a look.

412
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:26,440
Oh, just damn it all.

413
00:19:26,460 --> 00:19:27,100
Don't be shy.

414
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:30,200
Whoa, not bad.

415
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:32,280
What about this one?

416
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:35,040
Bet you could use this to stabilize your magic.

417
00:19:35,860 --> 00:19:38,340
Maybe, if it wasn't so ugly.

418
00:19:38,740 --> 00:19:40,820
Come on, it can't hurt to give it a try.

419
00:19:40,820 --> 00:19:55,940
You only have yourself to blame

420
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:57,500
for walking there in the first place.

421
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:00,520
Well, hello, lovely ladies.

422
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:02,440
What brings you here?

423
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:05,060
The black market can be quite dangerous.

424
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:08,040
It's no place for such delicate flowers to roam about.

425
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:10,940
Are you lost, perhaps?

426
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:13,900
As a magic knight, I'd be happy to escort you out.

427
00:20:14,320 --> 00:20:15,920
It would be no trouble in the least.

428
00:20:16,620 --> 00:20:18,100
Be gone with you, insect.

429
00:20:20,980 --> 00:20:21,500
Hey!

430
00:20:21,980 --> 00:20:24,100
Check this out, it's the best thing ever!

431
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:26,760
Not even you could be stupid enough

432
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:28,060
to buy something like that.

433
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:29,280
Kid talks and everything!

434
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:30,520
I stand corrected.

435
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:31,080
Listen!

436
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:33,240
Take this to your leader, human.

437
00:20:33,460 --> 00:20:33,900
Huh?

438
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,220
You worry me.

439
00:20:36,220 --> 00:20:37,800
Ha-ha!

440
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:39,280
No!

441
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:40,700
Him again!

442
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:42,240
Hey, I remember you!

443
00:20:42,540 --> 00:20:43,340
Ha-ha!

444
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:44,280
That's Seke!

445
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:44,780
Ha-ha!

446
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:46,360
How've you been?

447
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:46,760
Ha-ha!

448
00:20:47,020 --> 00:20:48,800
I told you, my name is...

449
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:49,060
Ha-ha!

450
00:20:49,280 --> 00:20:49,560
No!

451
00:20:49,700 --> 00:20:50,540
I mean, it's Seke!

452
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:52,060
Who's this?

453
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:54,500
We took the entrance exam together.

454
00:20:55,360 --> 00:20:57,520
Oh, so you're on the mantis squad.

455
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:59,960
The best-looking women here,

456
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:00,900
and they're with him?

457
00:21:00,900 --> 00:21:02,260
Hold on.

458
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:04,800
They're wearing black bulls' robes, too?

459
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:07,000
Stupid Osta!

460
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:10,260
I can't believe I'm actually jealous of a black bull!

461
00:21:10,780 --> 00:21:11,480
Damn him!

462
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:13,720
That runs the whole reason I wound up

463
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:15,640
in the praying mantises in the first place!

464
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:16,600
Ha-ha!

465
00:21:16,920 --> 00:21:18,580
I'll make him pay!

466
00:21:18,580 --> 00:21:19,380
Ha-ha!

467
00:21:19,380 --> 00:21:19,780
Ha-ha!

468
00:21:19,780 --> 00:21:19,820
Ha-ha!

469
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:19,980
Ha-ha!

470
00:21:29,980 --> 00:21:30,580
No!

471
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:31,060
Me!

472
00:21:31,180 --> 00:21:32,120
Get back here!

473
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:34,380
Those are my winnings, you fiend!

474
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:37,040
Give them back to me!

475
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:37,840
Ha!

476
00:21:44,680 --> 00:21:45,320
Ha!

477
00:21:45,940 --> 00:21:46,820
Ha!

478
00:21:46,820 --> 00:21:55,020
Wasn't there anybody who could come to stage?

479
00:21:55,020 --> 00:22:02,860
It's closed the quiet table in a limited environment

480
00:22:02,860 --> 00:22:11,820
The first voix continues to shine

481
00:22:11,820 --> 00:22:41,800
See you next time.

482
00:22:41,820 --> 00:23:11,800
See you next time.

483
00:23:11,820 --> 00:23:13,820
See you next time.

484
00:23:42,260 --> 00:23:44,300
Black Clover, page 12.

485
00:23:44,580 --> 00:23:45,880
The Wizard King saw.

486
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:48,260
My magic is never giving up.

487
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:49,000
Ha-ha!

